1443 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Making their homes within the hollow trunks of the Great Jiila trees\054 these Dwarves are native only to the wild\054 untamed forests of The Wild Hook\056 Very few have seen these Dwarves in person\054 and many do not believe them to truly exist\056 These Dwarves are one with nature\054 and highly peaceful\056 The Great Jiila trees have naturally hollow trunks\054 making a perfect living environment for the Canopy Dwarves\054 who spend much of their time high in the treetops gathering materials\054 keeping lookout\054 or hunting\056 Many have dedicated their lives to protecting and preserving the wonders of The Wild Hook and all of nature\047s wonders\056 Canopy Dwarves stand slightly smaller than normal Dwarves\054 standing around 2\0565 to 3 feet tall\056 If not for their bulky appearance and heavy facial hair\054 some Canopy Dwarves may even be mistaken for some of the even smaller races of Pliara\056 Their special connection with nature has granted them unique abilities that are uncommon in other Dwarves\056)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 1444 0 R
     /Pg 1116 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

