  >>
endobj

1445 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The most abundant dwarven folk in major cities\054 Hill Dwarves build massive\054 proud clans centered around specific trades\056 A single leader or a council guides each group\054 directing every member toward a shared purpose like mining\054 hunting\054 or smithing\056 Honor dictates their daily life\054 and a slight against one member offends the whole lineage\056 While they maintain strong ties with other civilized folk\054 their opinion of their marsh\055dwelling cousins is far harsher\056 Hill Dwarves know full well that Marsh Dwarves generally choose evil or selfish paths\054 abandoning the lawful structure that keeps dwarven society standing\056 Because of this\054 Hill Dwarves view them with deep suspicion and disdain\054 considering them a dark blight on the dwarven name rather than kin worth protecting\056\n\nTheir stout frames carry natural resilience\054 giving them the stamina to work long hours at the forge or stand their ground in conflict\056 Settling in bustling urban centers has made them more open to outside trade\054 yet they never lose their traditional edge or discipline\056 They approach their work with methodical precision\054 ensuring that anything forged or built by a Hill Dwarf lasts for generations\056 That unwavering work ethic earns them widespread respect among city leaders\054 who frequently rely on dwarven craftsmanship to strengthen urban defenses and fuel local economies\056 Hill Dwarves remain the industrious backbone of any settlement they inhabit\054 keeping ancient traditions alive while building lasting regional influence\056)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 1446 0 R
     /Pg 1116 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

